# Routh II.Art.143 — Poinsot's construction: the momental ellipsoid rolls on a
# fixed plane — dynamic notebook
#
# E. J. Routh, "The Advanced Part of a Treatise on the Dynamics of a System of
# Rigid Bodies", Part II (Macmillan, 6th ed. 1905), Art. 143: "To explain
# Poinsot's representation of the motion by means of the momental ellipsoid."
#
# THE CONSTRUCTION. Build the momental ellipsoid at the fixed point and extend
# the instantaneous axis to meet it. Routh shows that the tangent plane there is
#
#   * PARALLEL to the invariable plane, and
#   * at a CONSTANT distance from the centre
#
# so the ellipsoid rolls, without slipping, on a plane fixed in space -- and the
# angular velocity is proportional to the radius vector to the point of contact.
# The whole of torque-free rotation is that one picture.
#
# THE INVARIANT THAT MAKES IT TESTABLE. The constant distance is, up to the
# ellipsoid's scaling, the projection of the angular velocity onto the
# invariable line:
#
#     w . Lhat  =  (w . L) / |L|  =  2E / G
#
# because w . L is exactly twice the kinetic energy. Both E and G are constants
# of a torque-free motion (Arts. 140-142), so their ratio is one too -- and it
# is the constancy of THIS number, not of w itself, that makes the rolling
# contact possible. The angular velocity may swing about as much as it likes,
# but its shadow on the invariable line never moves.
#
# THE NUMBERS. A cuboid of mass 3 with half-extents (0.5, 1, 2) gives
# I = diag(5, 4.25, 1.25). Started tumbling at w = (0.3, 3, 0.1):
#
#     G = |L| = 12.838540610209558
#     E       = 19.35625
#     w . Lhat = 2E/G = 3.0153349337240685      <- the rolling height
#
# The cells print that projection repeatedly, beside |w| itself. The projection
# does not move; |w| does.
#
# SETUP NOTE. system.g_constant = 0 -- one body only here, but in any
# multi-body version pairwise gravity at the default G = 1 lets the bodies fall
# into the 1/r^2 singularity and ruins a rotational result for a translational
# reason.
#
# WHAT YOU WATCH: a box tumbling irregularly. Invisibly, a plane is fixed in
# space and the body's momental ellipsoid is rolling on it without slipping.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LAUNCH (run from the repository root: /Users/nsh/Developer/code/rust/rustSimulate)
#
#     posim_notebook routh_p2_poinsot_rolling
#
# or, without the shell alias, the always-available form:
#
#     cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/routh_p2_poinsot_rolling.posim
#
# The scene window opens in your browser. To start the simulation, press Start
# in that window, or type this at the In[] prompt in the terminal:
#
#     scene start
#
# If no browser should be launched (the URL is printed instead), use:
#
#     POSIM_NO_BROWSER=1 cargo run -p posim --release -- --notebook dynamic_notebooks/routh_p2_poinsot_rolling.posim
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

set system.g_constant = 0
set system.rtol = 1e-13
set system.atol = 1e-15

new cuboid { mass = 3, half_extents = [0.5, 1, 2], angular_velocity = [0.3, 3, 0.1] }

get obj0.inertia_tensor
norm(obj0.angular_momentum)
energy
# the rolling height 2E/G, and the angular velocity's own magnitude
dot(obj0.angular_velocity, obj0.angular_momentum) / norm(obj0.angular_momentum)
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)

run 2 steps 2
dot(obj0.angular_velocity, obj0.angular_momentum) / norm(obj0.angular_momentum)
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)
run 2 steps 2
dot(obj0.angular_velocity, obj0.angular_momentum) / norm(obj0.angular_momentum)
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)
run 3 steps 3
dot(obj0.angular_velocity, obj0.angular_momentum) / norm(obj0.angular_momentum)
norm(obj0.angular_velocity)
reset

set system.g_constant = 0
set system.rtol = 1e-13
set system.atol = 1e-15
new cuboid { mass = 3, half_extents = [0.5, 1, 2], angular_velocity = [0.3, 3, 0.1] }

scene create
scene set_time_step 0.03
